@baseUrl = https://localhost:7156
# Replace these 0 values only with IDs of records YOU create for the demo.
@newCategoryId = 0
@newProductId = 0
@newCustomerId = 0
@newOrderId = 0

### 1. List products (optional LINQ filters)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?search=Logitech

### 2. Product detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{newProductId}}

### 3. Create product after creating a category
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Presentation Mouse","description":"USB","price":25.50,"stockQuantity":10,"categoryId":{{newCategoryId}}}

### 4. Update product
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{newProductId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Presentation Mouse Updated","description":"USB","price":29.50,"stockQuantity":10,"categoryId":{{newCategoryId}}}

### 5. Delete your demo product after deleting its demo orders
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/products/{{newProductId}}

### 6. List categories
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories

### 7. Category detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/categories/{{newCategoryId}}

### 8. Create category; copy returned id into newCategoryId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/categories
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Presentation Category","description":"University demonstration"}

### 9. Update category
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/categories/{{newCategoryId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Presentation Category Updated","description":"University demonstration"}

### 10. Delete your empty demo category
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/categories/{{newCategoryId}}

### 11. List customers
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers

### 12. Customer detail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{newCustomerId}}

### 13. Create customer; use a fresh email each demo
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{"firstName":"Ana","lastName":"Gelashvili","email":"presentation.ana@example.com","phone":"+995555020202"}

### 14. Update customer
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{newCustomerId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"firstName":"Ana","lastName":"Updated","email":"presentation.ana@example.com"}

### 15. Delete your demo customer after deleting its orders
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/customers/{{newCustomerId}}

### 16. List orders
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders

### 17. Order detail with order items
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{newOrderId}}

### 18. Create order; copy returned id into newOrderId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"customerId":{{newCustomerId}},"items":[{"productId":{{newProductId}},"quantity":2}]}

### 19. Cancel order (stock restored once)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{newOrderId}}/status
Content-Type: application/json

{"status":"Cancelled"}

### 20. Delete your cancelled demo order
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/orders/{{newOrderId}}

### External integration (additional operation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/exchange-rates?baseCurrency=USD&targetCurrency=GEL

### Validation example: 400, no record created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Invalid","price":0,"stockQuantity":-1,"categoryId":{{newCategoryId}}}
